=== CRITICAL RULES ===

--- Message Structure ---
1. Each message must contain "version": "v0.9" and exactly ONE message type key. Never combine multiple message types in one message.
2. The output must be valid JSONL — one JSON object per line, no trailing commas, no comments.

--- Message Ordering ---
3. A createSurface message MUST be sent before any updateComponents or updateDataModel messages for the same surfaceId.
4. Once created, a surface's surfaceId and catalogId are fixed. To change them, delete and recreate the surface.

--- Component Tree Structure ---
5. Components are a FLAT LIST (adjacency list model). Tree structure is built via ID references. NEVER nest component definitions inline.
6. Exactly ONE component MUST have id: "root". This is the root of the component tree.
7. All component IDs must be UNIQUE within a surface.
8. All child/children references must point to component IDs that exist in the components array.
9. Card uses "child" (single ComponentId). Row, Column, List use "children" (ChildList). Modal uses "trigger" and "content" (both ComponentId). Tabs uses "tabs" array with "child" per tab.
10. Use "weight" property ONLY on direct children of Row or Column.

--- Data Binding ---
11. Data bindings use JSON Pointers: {"path": "/some/data/path"} for absolute paths (starting with /). Absolute paths always resolve from the root of the data model.
12. Relative paths (no leading /) are ONLY used inside collection scope templates (ChildList template objects). When a container uses a template ChildList with a path (e.g., "/users"), components inside that template use relative paths (e.g., "name") which resolve to /users/0/name, /users/1/name, etc.
13. Components inside a collection scope can still access the root data model using absolute paths.

--- Two-Way Binding & Input Components ---
14. Input components (TextField, CheckBox, Slider, ChoicePicker, DateTimeInput) establish two-way binding when their value uses a data path. User input immediately updates the LOCAL data model — no network request is sent.
15. Other components bound to the same path reactively update when input changes the local data model.
16. The updated data model is sent to the server ONLY when a user action is triggered. Use the action's "context" to reference data paths that should be sent.

--- Actions ---
17. An Action must be EITHER {"event": {...}} OR {"functionCall": {...}} — never both in the same action object.
18. Server actions (event) send an event name and optional context to the server. Context values can be literals or data bindings.
19. Local actions (functionCall) execute client-side functions like openUrl.

--- Validation & Checks ---
20. CheckRule uses the structure: {"condition": <DynamicBoolean>, "message": "<string>"}. The condition wraps the function call; do NOT put the function call properties (call, args) directly on the CheckRule.
20a. A field is REQUIRED if ANY of the following are true:
     - The intent explicitly states "Required" or "required" for that field (even if followed by "(not specified)").
     - The field is the primary purpose of the form (e.g., name fields on a personal details form).
     - The field is a legal/consent checkbox (e.g., terms acceptance, privacy policy).
     Always add a `required` CheckRule to every required field.
21. For input components, check failures produce error messages displayed on the component.

--- Type Conversion ---
22. When non-string values are interpolated: numbers/booleans become their string representation, null/undefined become empty string "", objects/arrays are JSON-stringified.

